                    <desc_content>
                        <paragraph>Converts <literal classes="xref py py-obj">value</literal> to Hydra-supported type or to a config whose fields are recursively supported by <reference internal="1" refid="hydra_zen.BuildsFn._make_hydra_compatible" reftitle="hydra_zen.BuildsFn._make_hydra_compatible"><literal classes="xref py py-obj">_make_hydra_compatible</literal></reference>. Otherwise
                            raises <literal classes="xref py py-obj">HydraZenUnsupportedPrimitiveError</literal>.</paragraph>
                        <paragraph>Override this method to add support for adding auto-config support to custom
                            types.</paragraph>
                        <rubric>Notes</rubric>
                        <definition_list>
                            <definition_list_item>
                                <term>Hydra supports the following types:</term>
                                <definition>
                                    <paragraph><reference internal="0" reftitle="(in Python v3.15)" refuri="https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#bool"><literal classes="xref py py-obj">bool</literal></reference>, <reference internal="0" reftitle="(in Python v3.15)" refuri="https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None"><literal classes="xref py py-obj">None</literal></reference>, <reference internal="0" reftitle="(in Python v3.15)" refuri="https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int"><literal classes="xref py py-obj">int</literal></reference>, <reference internal="0" reftitle="(in Python v3.15)" refuri="https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float"><literal classes="xref py py-obj">float</literal></reference>, <reference internal="0" reftitle="(in Python v3.15)" refuri="https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str"><literal classes="xref py py-obj">str</literal></reference>, <reference internal="0" reftitle="(in Python v3.15)" refuri="https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#bytes"><literal classes="xref py py-obj">bytes</literal></reference>, <reference internal="0" reftitle="(in Python v3.15)" refuri="https://docs.python.org/3/library/pathlib.html#pathlib.Path"><literal classes="xref py py-obj">pathlib.Path</literal></reference>,
                                        <reference internal="0" reftitle="(in Python v3.15)" refuri="https://docs.python.org/3/library/dataclasses.html#dataclasses.MISSING"><literal classes="xref py py-obj">dataclasses.MISSING</literal></reference>. As well as lists, tuples, dicts, and omegaconf
                                        containers containing the above.</paragraph>
                                </definition>
                            </definition_list_item>
                        </definition_list>
